Prior art
---------

This project credits oil-oil/selector (https://github.com/oil-oil/selector) as
prior art for three ideas it builds on:

  * delivering an element-selection tool as a self-contained `javascript:`
    bookmarklet rather than a browser extension;
  * the locator ladder — trying progressively weaker selector strategies and
    keeping the first one that identifies the element;
  * the getDisplayMedia screenshot sequence — request a display-capture stream
    from a user gesture, take one frame, crop it to the element's rect.

ui-selector is a new repository, not a fork, and shares no code with
oil-oil/selector. All three ideas above are reimplemented here from documented
Web API behaviour (DOM, CSSOM, Selectors, and Screen Capture).

If any file in this repository later adapts upstream code directly, that file
will carry upstream's MIT attribution in its own header.
